    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `customerCode` assignment on `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` + a global 4-digit sequence one greater than the current owner count).\n\nI kept structural impact low by adding a single new, self-contained step rather than growing any existing function or class:\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 one tiny function (no surrounding class complexity to hold) that computes the code and mutates the entity in place. This follows the AGENTS.md `Assign<E>` convention.\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignCode` step between `checkTelephone` and `save`, so the code is computed *before* persistence (the owner isn't yet counted \u2192 `count + 1`).\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `customerCode` `@Column` field with a plain getter/setter.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into the GET response.\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (the test profile uses HSQLDB with `ddl-auto=none`) and padded the positional seed inserts.\n\nDeliberate choices:\n- I did **not** fold the logic into `SaveOwner`, because it's shared with the PUT pipeline \u2014 that would wrongly reassign codes on every update.\n- I put `AssignCustomerCode` before `save` so `findAll().size()` reflects the count *excluding* the new owner, giving the required monotonic sequence across creates.\n\nThe single test `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (and the whole suite) passes: `SMI-\u2026` / `JON-\u2026` prefixes and consecutive sequence numbers verified.",
